@@ -24,6 +24,13 @@ The user has asked for a **retrospective**. You are suggesting improvements to t
 
 4. Present these candidates to the user, in order of severity.
 
+5. Hand off the fixes. This skill finds the candidates. It doesn't build them. End with the next command for each kind, so the user can run it:
+
+   - **Mechanical** mistakes the agent repeated (a check, a type, a lint rule would stop them) → `/correct`. It fixes each class at the highest level that works and proves the check fails on the real past mistake. Name the classes you found so it can start from them.
+   - A skill's instructions sent the agent the wrong way, or a long run taught a recipe worth keeping → `/reflect`, which turns the lesson into a skill edit.
+   - The root problem is a missing seam or a shallow module → `/improve-codebase-architecture`.
+   - The agent misunderstood a domain term → `/grill-with-docs` to fix `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
